HST Office: Page Setup in Sheets moves toward Excel's Page, Header/Footer, Sheet order
(owner-approved Microsoft Office parity for beta.5).

- Tabs: page, header, footer, sheet, then borders and background; page ids unchanged. The dialog opens on
  the page tab unless a new style is being named; the organizer tab stays first (added by SfxStyleDialogController).
- The sheet tab gets Excel's Print Titles first: rows and columns to repeat on every page of the current
  sheet, applied on OK only. Text fields take $1:$2 and $A:$B; the existing Print Ranges dialog still works.

Scaling stays on the sheet tab and margins stay on the page tab: moving them means changing the page
shared with Writer and Slides (cui/uiconfig/ui/pageformatpage.ui).

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-dialogs-sheets.py (page-setup).
